From: "opus-pr2-patch (Claude)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:04:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] workflow: commit the heartbeat even before data/history
 exists (D-4)

Step 5 ran `git add -A data/history data/status.json`
(update-lightning.yml:102). While data/history does not exist (PR #2 ships
none; it appears only after the first successful archive write) git aborts
with "fatal: pathspec 'data/history' did not match any files", exit 128,
nothing staged, so every failed bootstrap run lost its status.json
heartbeat. The two paths are now added separately, data/history only when
it exists.

tests/test_workflow.py runs the step's own shell (extracted from the YAML,
bash -e as on Actions) in a throwaway repository with a local bare origin.
test_status_is_committed_when_data_history_does_not_exist_yet fails before
with exit 128. test-lightning.yml now also triggers on changes to
update-lightning.yml so these tests run when the workflow changes.

